wishnode.net — Contract and Grant Ledger page content phext (phexts/contract-ledger.phext). Source of truth for the Contract and Grant Ledger page. Task 34.6.6/7.7.10/7.6.10. See docs/COORDINATE-MAP.md.Contract & Grant Ledger — Exocortexia | Phext, Inc.Contract and Grant LedgerA feeder and checker for the Nebraska State Contracts Database · Neb. Rev. Stat. § 84-602.04SUMMARY (plain English — rendered first)The Contract and Grant Ledger keeps your office's contract list and checks it against the state's public contract list. It flags contracts that are missing from the public list and warns you before a contract runs out. It is for agency staff who must post contracts under Nebraska law.Click the button below to open the live demo. You will see the list of contracts. The alerts list shows which contracts end soon. It also flags the ones that are not on the state public list.This demo is open to all, and it uses made-up data. No sign-in is needed, and no real files are here. In a real setup for your office, staff sign in first through edit.phext.io, and the files are your own real ones.What it doesState contracts must be posted in the public State Contracts Database. In real life, the two lists drift apart. Posts get missed. A change raises the amount a contract allows, but the public list does not show it.This tool keeps your side of the list and checks it against the public side. The gaps become a short work list, not a surprise at audit time.Changes that never rewrite the pastWhen a contract changes, the change is a new note tied to the first record. The first record is never changed. The true amount is the first amount plus each change. You can trace the full path from start to now.Each contract is grouped by how much time is left: past its end date, or ending in the next 30, 60, or 90 days. Staff see what needs work soon.A contract that is in your records but not in the public database gets a clear flag: MISSING FROM PUBLIC DATABASE. That flag is the work list — the posts to chase.The demo holds 60 made-up contracts. That is large enough for the drift to show at a glance: missed posts, changes not shown in public, and end dates that crept up.What the law saysNebraska law (§ 84-602.04, passed as LB 429 in 2011) set up the public State Contracts Database. Agencies must make their contracts part of that public record.The public search is at statecontracts.nebraska.gov.The law is met only when what your office holds matches what the public can see. That match is the whole job of this tool.Check the current law text and any value limits before you cite them in a formal bid. This page is a guide, not legal advice.Full statute sheet: see the Contract Ledger part of the statutes phext on this site. The page link reads “How the Contract Ledger matches Nebraska law.”Good to knowThis tool does not replace the state database. It feeds it and checks it.All 60 contracts in the demo are made up.Each figure on screen can be worked out again from the stored records. Nothing is typed in by hand.The suite is checked by 84 automated tests. Eight of them check this program, and they cover the change math and the end-date groups.Ask about a pilotAsk about a pilot for your office. Use the form on this site — the link says “Ask about a pilot.” Tell us which program you are interested in and what your office needs. When you send the form, you get a tracking code. Keep it. You can use it on this site to check the state of your request at any time. We read every request, and a person from Phext, Inc. replies. We will talk through what a small pilot would look like for your office. There is no cost to ask, and asking does not sign you up for anything.Links on this page (descriptive labels)Read the Contract Ledger source code (for programmers) — Source tree in the Exocortexia repositoryHow the Contract Ledger matches Nebraska law — Statute sheet, also held in phexts/statutes.phextFOR TECHNICAL STAFF — not main copy. Component: apps/contract-ledger · Default port: 8803 · Tests: 8 in this app, 69 workspace-wide · Sign-in: edit.phext.io SSO when configured; open demo mode otherwise · Source: github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia/tree/exo/apps/contract-ledger · Statute sheet source: docs/contract-ledger-statute.md.Original page text before the plain-English rewrite (provenance):
